  "question": {
    "text": "An alternating voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>220</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>100</mn><mi>π</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> volt is applied to a purely resistive load of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math>. The time taken for the current to rise from half of the peak value to the peak value is:"
